@flexiarg operator/the-record-carries-the-spec
@title The Record Carries The Spec — 'As Mentioned' Is A Pointer
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-b8sJ89 turn-fHQyvl
@parent futon-theory/single-source-of-truth
@context The operator authorises the next step of work whose content was already established earlier in the shared record.

! conclusion: Issue the instruction as a pointer ('as mentioned', 'as before', 'the next one') and let the shared record carry the specification.

  + IF:
    The instruction would be a verbatim repeat of something already said and visible to both parties.

  + HOWEVER:
    Restating the spec wastes the operator's turn and invites drift between two copies; but a bare pointer fails if the referent is ambiguous — the move only works when the record holds exactly one thing it can mean.

  + THEN:
    Issue the instruction as a pointer ('as mentioned', 'as before', 'the next one') and let the shared record carry the specification.

  + BECAUSE:
    The parent's norm — one authoritative copy, everything else a reference — applied to operator instructions: the earlier statement is the source of truth for what the repair is, and 'as mentioned' is the citation of it rather than a second, diverging copy.
